# Claude Code OAuth token — get one by running `claude setup-token` on your host.
# Lets the agent use your Claude subscription instead of an API key.
CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=
# Or use an Anthropic API key instead — uncomment and fill in:
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# GitHub token — the agent uses it to read and manage GitHub Issues.
# Leave EMPTY to inherit the host's `gh` login: sandcastle falls back to
# process.env for any key present-but-blank here, and `bun run sandcastle`
# injects `$(gh auth token)`. Nothing is written to disk and it never goes stale.
# Fill it in only to use a narrower token than your `gh` login — a fine-grained
# PAT (https://github.com/settings/personal-access-tokens/new) needs
# Issues (Read and write) + Metadata (Read). Note: the agent also needs to read
# issues and the repo, so Contents (Read) is worth granting too.
GH_TOKEN=
